    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/nuimrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=044143": {
      "title": "Academic Programmes Officer, Permanent, Admissions and Student Recruitment Department, Maynooth University",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/10/2026 Job Title : Academic Programmes Officer Department : Admissions Office Vacancy ID : 044143 Closing Date : 11-Oct-2026 The Role Maynooth University is committed to a strategy in which the primary University goals of excellent research and scholarship and outstanding education are interlinked and equally valued. We are seeking an Academic Programmes Officer to contribute to the administration, coordination and continuous enhancement of postgraduate recruitment, admissions and programme development activity. The post holder will take primary responsibility for the coordination and administration of Springboard+, Human Capital Initiative (HCI) funded programmes and Micro-Credential programmes, serving as a key liaison between academic departments, Registry and Admissions team. Reporting to the Senior Student Recruitment Manager (Postgraduate), the post holder will also contribute to the development University's academic portfolio through the provision of market intelligence and data analysis, as well as to the wider activities of the Postgraduate Recruitment Team. Postgraduate recruitment is a key priority within the University’s Strategic Plan 2023–2028, and the role offers the opportunity to contribute to a high-impact area with strong visibility across the institution. Salary Administrative Officer II (2026): €47,387 – €67,129 p.a. (9 points) Appointments will be made in accordance with public sector pay provisions. Closing Date: 23:30hrs (local Irish time) on Sunday, 11th of October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified above. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. Late applications will not be accepted. Maynooth University is an equal opportunities employer The position is subject to the Statutes of the University"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/nuimrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=044243": {
      "title": "Administrative Officer (Specified Purpose Contract)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/10/2026 Job Title : Administrative Officer Department : Freedom of Information/Data Protection Vacancy ID : 044243 Closing Date : 11-Oct-2026 The University’s Data Protection and Freedom of Information Office is legally responsible for ensuring that the University is compliant with the GDPR (General Data Protection Regulation), Data Protection legislation and Freedom of Information legislation. The Office sits within the Governance Directorate and acts as a champion for Data Protection compliance and create awareness and knowledge across the University. The Office is responsible for assisting staff, students and members of the public in exercising their rights under the legislation. We are seeking to appoint an Administrative Officer, Data Protection/ Freedom of Information Office. Reporting to the DPO/FOI Officer, the successful candidate will be responsible for carrying out required tasks to ensure compliance throughout the University with relevant legislation and supporting the functions that are legally required of the DP/FOI Office. Administrative Officer 1 (2026) Salary Scale: €60,410 – €86,192 p.a. (9 points) Appointments will be made in accordance with public sector pay provisions. Closing Date: 23:30hrs (local Irish time) on Sunday, 11th October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified above. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. Late applications will not be accepted . Maynooth University is an equal opportunities employer The position is subject to the Statutes of the University"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/nuimrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=044403": {
      "title": "Administrative Officer II (Conferring), Specified Purpose, Registry: Examinations & Assessment Office",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/10/2026 Job Title : Administrative Officer II Department : Examinations Office Vacancy ID : 044403 Closing Date : 25-Oct-2026 The Examinations & Assessment Office requires a highly organised and efficient administrator to to support the work of a very busy office. Among the chief responsibilities, the appointee will co-ordinate and organise the University conferring ceremonies, supervise the PhD submission process and be instrumental in developing a new exam paper management process. They will also be responsible for the coordination and distribution of the Universities annual prizes and certificates to all graduates. The person appointed must be a team player and have the ability to communicate confidently and effectively. They will work with the existing Examinations & Assessment team to deliver enhancements to the student experience and to practices as appropriate. The successful candidate will be organised and logical, with an ability to develop and manage detailed processes. They will work to lead part of the team in a deadline driven office, to support the delivery of key assessment-related services to students and staff. Administrative Officer II (2026) Salary Scale: €47,387 – €67,129 p.a. (9 points) Appointments will be made in accordance with public sector pay provisions. Closing Date: 23:30hrs (local Irish time) on Sunday, 25th October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified above. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. Late applications will not be accepted. Maynooth University is an equal opportunities employer The position is subject to the Statutes of the University"
