    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/nuimrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=044204": {
      "title": "Assistant Lecturer in Human Geography (Specified Purpose Contract), Department of Geography",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/10/2026 Job Title : Assistant Lecturer Department : Geography Vacancy ID : 044204 Closing Date : 18-Oct-2026 Maynooth University is committed to a strategy in which the primary University goals of excellent research and scholarship and outstanding education are interlinked and equally valued. We are seeking an excellent academic to join our staff as an Assistant Lecturer in Human Geography. The person appointed will have a proven record of teaching, research and publication, appropriate to career stage. They will be expected to make a strong contribution to the teaching programme of the Department and undertake teaching duties on the Department’s undergraduate and postgraduate programmes as well as the supervision of Master’s and PhD students. The appointee will be expected to build a strong research profile, that supports the University’s research strategy including affiliating to the Research Institutes, where appropriate and working with colleagues on national and international research. The appointee will be expected to sustain and conduct research, engage in scholarship of quality and substance and generate publications of international standard. Salary: Assistant Lecturer (2026): €43,025 - €45,240 p.a. (2 points) Appointments will be made in accordance with public sector pay provisions. Closing Date: 23:30hrs (local Irish time) on Sunday, 18th October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified above. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. Late applications will not be accepted. Maynooth University is an equal opportunities employer The position is subject to the Statutes of the University ______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________ Tá Ollscoil Mhá Nuad tiomanta do straitéis ina ndéantar príomhspriocanna na hOllscoile maidir le taighde agus scoláireacht den scoth agus oideachas sármhaith a idirnascadh agus ina léirítear an meas céanna ar an dá ghné. Táimid ag lorg acadóir den scoth le bheith páirteach lenár bhfoireann mar Léachtóir Cúnta i dTíreolaíocht Dhaonna. Beidh cuntas cruthaithe ag an té a cheapfar ar theagasc, ar thaighde agus ar fhoilsiú, atá oiriúnach do staid a g(h)airme. Beifear ag súil go rannchuideoidh an té a cheapfar go suntasach le clár teagaisc na Roinne agus go dtabharfaidh siad faoi dhualgais teagaisc ar chláir fochéime agus iarchéime na Roinne, chomh maith le maoirseacht a dhéanamh ar mhic léinn Máistreachta agus PhD. Beifear ag súil go bhforbróidh an té a cheapfar próifíl láidir taighde a thacóidh le straitéis taighde na hOllscoile, lena n-áirítear cleamhnú leis na hInstitiúidí Taighde, nuair is cuí, agus comhoibriú le comhghleacaithe ar thaighde náisiúnta agus idirnáisiúnta. Beifear ag súil go leanfaidh an té a cheapfar ar aghaidh le taighde a dhéanamh agus taighde a chur i gcrích, go rachaidh siad i mbun scoláireachta ar ardchaighdeán agus a bhfuil doimhneacht inti, agus go gcruthóidh siad foilseacháin ar chaighdeán idirnáisiúnta. Tuarastal Léachtóir Cúnta (2026): €43,025 - €45,240 p.a. (2 pointe) De réir fhorálacha pá na hearnála poiblí a dhéanfar ceapacháin. Dáta Deiridh: 23:30 (am na hÉireann) ar an Domhnach, 18 Deireadh Fómhair 2026 Caithfear iarratais a chur isteach faoin dáta deiridh agus faoin am a shonraítear thuas. Cealóidh an córas go huathoibríoch iarratais atá fós idir lámha ag an am deiridh ar an dáta deiridh sonraithe. Ní ghlacfar le hiarratais mhalla. Is fostóir comhdheiseanna í Ollscoil Mhá Nuad Tá an post seo faoi réir Reachtanna na hOllscoile"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/nuimrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=044063": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor / Lecturer in Music Technology, Specified Purpose, Department of Music",
      "description": "Closing Date: 14/10/2026 Job Title : AP/Lecturer in Music Technology Department : Music Vacancy ID : 044063 Closing Date : 14-Oct-2026 We are seeking an excellent academic to join our staff as an Assistant Professor / Lecturer in Music Technology. The person appointed will have a proven record of teaching, research and publication, appropriate to career stage, and will contribute to the development of Music Technology across the Department’s undergraduate and postgraduate programmes. The appointee will have a track record of research and publication demonstrating substantive technical expertise in computational and/or interactive music technologies, with particular expertise in areas such as interactive music systems and new interfaces for musical expression, including haptic, gestural and sensor-based interaction, physical computing; embedded systems audio programming; real-time signal processing; digital audio systems; spatial and immersive audio technologies. The appointee will be expected to make a strong contribution to the teaching programme of the Department and undertake teaching duties on the Department’s undergraduate and postgraduate programmes, as well as the supervision of MA and PhD students. They will play an active role in developing and shaping the Music Technology curriculum in response to developments in the field and to their own areas of expertise. They will also be expected to contribute to teaching in core studio and audio-production techniques, including recording, microphone techniques, mixing and DAW-based workflows. Candidates with research or creative-practice expertise in recording and music production will be well placed to contribute to the development of this area. The appointee will be expected to build a strong research profile, that supports the University’s research strategy including affiliating to the Research Institutes, where appropriate and working with colleagues on national and international research. The appointee will be expected to sustain and conduct research, engage in scholarship of quality and substance and generate publications of international standard. Salary Scale: Assistant Professor / Lecturer: €66,055 – €104,600 p.a. (7 points) Assistant Lecturer: €43,025 – €73,445 p.a. (14 points) Closing Date: 23:30hrs (local Irish time) on Wednesday, 14th October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified above. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. Late applications will not be accepted. Maynooth University is an equal opportunities employer The position is subject to the Statutes of the University"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/nuimrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=044283": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor/Lecturer in Education, Temporary Contract, Department of Education, Maynooth University",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/10/2026 Job Title : AP / Lecturer in Education Department : Education Vacancy ID : 044283 Closing Date : 25-Oct-2026 The Role Maynooth University is committed to a strategy in which the primary University goals of excellent research and scholarship and outstanding education are interlinked and equally valued. We are seeking an excellent academic to join our staff as a Lecturer in Education (with Specialism in Education Guidance Counselling). The candidate should have a Doctorate in Education (or cognate area) or be nearing completion of their Doctorate. The preferred candidate will be expected to make a strong contribution to the teaching and research programmes of the Department, undertaking teaching duties on the Department’s Education Guidance Counselling programme and the Initial Teacher Education programmes at both the undergraduate and postgraduate levels. They will also be expected to contribute to Master’s and Doctoral level modules and supervision as well as conduct placement supervision if required. They will have the theoretical and professional knowledge required to develop student guidance counsellors in Education Guidance Counselling and support their practice in classrooms and schools. Experience of working in teacher and counsellor education and researching into school-based settings is highly desirable. The preferred candidate will also be able to work collaboratively in supporting the collegial work of the Department and to assume administrative and course leadership duties, in particular on Education Guidance Counselling and as required on the Department’s programmes. The appointee will be expected to build a strong research profile that supports the University’s research strategy, including affiliating to the Research Institutes, where appropriate, and working with colleagues on national and international research. The appointee will be expected to sustain and conduct research, engage in scholarship of quality and substance, undertake engaged research, and generate publications of international standard. They will be expected to supervise research students up to doctoral level. The person appointed will have a record of teaching, research, and publication, appropriate to career stage. Salary Assistant Professor / Lecturer: €66,055 – € 104,600 p.a. (7 points) Assistant Lecturer)*: €43,025 – € 73,445 p.a. (14 points) Appointments will be made in accordance with public sector pay provisions. Closing Date: 23:30hrs (local Irish time) on Sunday 25th October 2026 Please note all applications must be made via our Online Recruitment Portal at the following link: https://www.maynoothuniversity.ie/human-resources/vacancies Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified above. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. Late applications will not be accepted. Maynooth University is an equal opportunities employer The position is subject to the Statutes of the University"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/nuimrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=044363": {
      "title": "Employability and Skill Development Co-ordinator (Specified Purpose) Office of Student Skills and Success",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/10/2026 Job Title : Employability and Skill Dev. Coordinator Department : Student Skills & Success Vacancy ID : 044363 Closing Date : 18-Oct-2026 Maynooth University is committed to a strategy in which the primary University goals of excellent research and scholarship and outstanding education are interlinked and equally valued. The Careers and Employability Service (CES), within Student Skills and Success in the Office of Students and Learning, is seeking a motivated, collaborative and proactive Employability and Skill Development Coordinator. Reporting to the Experiential Learning Officer, the successful candidate will contribute to the design, delivery and continuous enhancement of delivery of the extensive experiential learning and employability UpSkill programme within the Careers and Employability Service. It encompasses a diverse range of responsibilities and actively supports core University wide experiential learning programmes including; Maynooth University Student Experience (MUSE), Summer Programme of Undergraduate Research (SPUR), MU Micro-Internships and Alumni Career Mentoring Programme and the Skills for Success Module. The role involves working collaboratively with students, academic colleagues, employers and external partners to develop and promote high-quality experiential learning opportunities. The postholder will support students at all stages of their university journey by enabling skills development, career readiness, informed career decision-making and progression. The position contributes directly to the implementation of Maynooth University's Strategic Plan 2023-2028 and its mission to “imagine and create better futures for all”, supporting the development of highly employable graduates who are equipped to become the next generation of creators, innovators and decision-makers. This is an exciting opportunity for an individual with strong communication, stakeholder engagement and project management skills who is passionate about student development and enhancing graduate employability. Salary: Administrative Officer AOII (2026) €47,387 – €67,129 p.a. (9 points) Appointments will be made in accordance with public sector pay provisions. Closing Date: 23:30hrs (local Irish time) on Sunday, 18th October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified above. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. Late applications will not be accepted. Maynooth University is an equal opportunities employer The position is subject to the Statutes of the University"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/nuimrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=044383": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant (Specified Purpose Contract)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/10/2026 Job Title : Executive Assistant Department : Examinations Office Vacancy ID : 044383 Closing Date : 18-Oct-2026 The Examinations & Assessment Office are seeking an organised and efficient administrator to support the work of a very busy office.The role is varied and involves operational and administrative duties and requires a high level of IT and data handling skills. Applications are therefore, invited for a maternity leave (specified purpose contract) as an Executive Assistant within the Examinations, Assessment & Conferring function. Among the chief responsibilities, the appointee will support the accurate and agile management of the processes and documentation surrounding university exams, conferring ceremonies, and the administration of supports to students. The person appointed must be a team player and have the ability to communicate confidently and effectively. They will work as part of a team in a deadline driven office, to support the delivery of key assessment-related services to students and staff. Executive Assistant (2026) Salary Scale: €32,855 – €49,419 p.a. (13 points) Appointments will be made in accordance with public sector pay provisions. Closing Date: 23:30hrs (local Irish time) on Sunday, 18th October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified above. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. Late applications will not be accepted. Maynooth University is an equal opportunities employer The position is subject to the Statutes of the University"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/nuimrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=044203": {
      "title": "Executive Dean of Science and Engineering",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/10/2026 Job Title : Executive Dean of Science & Engineering Department : Office: Science & Engineering Vacancy ID : 044203 Closing Date : 30-Oct-2026 Maynooth University is an internationally recognised institution and Ireland’s fastest growing university. One of four constituent universities of the National University of Ireland, Maynooth University is in the top 90 global Times Higher Education Young University Rankings 2024. With over 17,000 students and 1,200 staff based across three Faculties, Maynooth offers a range of programmes at undergraduate, postgraduate and doctoral level in science and engineering, arts and humanities, and social sciences, including business, law, and education. Maynooth’s unique collegial culture fosters an interdisciplinary approach to research, tackling some of the most fundamental challenges facing society today. Maynooth University is seeking to appoint an Executive Dean of the Faculty of Science and Engineering. As a member of the University Executive, the Executive Dean will lead the development of the Faculty, working with key internal and external stakeholders to raise the profile, reputation, and performance of Maynooth University via the Faculty’s educational and research strengths. The Executive Dean will play a pivotal role in shaping the future direction of the Faculty, maintaining and enhancing the excellence, reputation, and growth of its existing Schools and Departments, while leading the establishment of a new School of Health and Medicine as a core strategic priority for the University. The successful appointee will demonstrate strong experience with operational and strategic leadership in a relevant environment combined with an excellent track record in research and teaching in an academic discipline aligning with current and future plans for the Faculty, which includes science, engineering, and health. They will have a key role in promoting and facilitating cross-university opportunities for teaching, research and engagement, and will have the ambassadorial skills to represent the Faculty and University externally at a national and international level. Maynooth University will be supported in this appointment process by the executive search firm Perrett Laver. Enquiries can be made directly to Callum Conway, callum.conway@perrettlaver.com.Further information and applications can be made via https://PLusPortal.PerrettLaver.com quoting reference 7839 . The closing date for applications will be Friday, 30th October 2026 . Applications should consist of a full curriculum vitae detailing academic and professional qualifications and experience. CVs should be accompanied by a covering letter describing briefly how candidates meet the criteria outlined in the job description, why the appointment is of interest and what they believe they can bring to the role. Candidates who are longlisted by the Committee will be invited to first round interview with Perrett Laver in mid to late November. Shortlisted candidates will be invited for formal interviews with the Selection Committee in early December. The appointment will be made subject to satisfactory references, and the formal interview process may include additional assessments. Perrett Laver is a Data Controller and a Data Processor, as defined under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). Our legal basis for much of our data processing activity is ‘Legitimate Interests’. You have the right to object to us processing your data in this way. For more information about this, your rights, and our approach to Data Protection and Privacy, please visit our website: http://www.perrettlaver.com/information/privacy-policy */ .*"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/nuimrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=044083": {
      "title": "Faculty Events Officer, Permanent, Faculty of Arts and Humanities",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/10/2026 Job Title : Faculty Events Officer Department : Office: Arts & Humanities Vacancy ID : 044083 Closing Date : 11-Oct-2026 Maynooth University is committed to a strategy in which the primary University goals of excellent research and scholarship and outstanding education are interlinked and equally valued. We are seeking a Faculty Events Officer for the Faculty of Arts and Humanities to organise and administer faculty events over the academic year, with particular focus on, and responsibility for, the annual Arts & Minds Festival. The role will be hosted in the Dean’s Office and will report to the Dean of the Faculty of Arts and Humanities working closely with the University Events team within the External Relations Office. The Faculty Events Officer will be capable of managing multiple events in different stages of execution, promoting the events, analysing their success through both data and qualitative measures, and of thinking strategically about how to devise events that serve the Faculty’s and University’s strategic interests and objectives for alumni engagement and philanthropy. Salary Scale: Administrative Officer I: €60,410– €86,192 p.a. (9 points) Closing Date: 23:30hrs (local Irish time) on Sunday, 11th October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified above. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. Late applications will not be accepted. Maynooth University is an equal opportunities employer The position is subject to the Statutes of the University"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/nuimrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=044103": {
      "title": "Feidhmeannach Riaracháin TEG (Conradh sainchuspóra), Lárionad na Gaeilge",
      "description": "Closing Date: 08/11/2026 Job Title : Feidhmeannach Riaracháin TEG Department : School of Celtic Studies Vacancy ID : 044103 Closing Date : 08-Nov-2026 Tá Ollscoil Mhá Nuad tiomanta do straitéis ina bhfuil príomhspriocanna na hOllscoile, taighde agus scoláireacht, agus oideachas den scoth, fite fuaite ina chéile agus ina léirítear an meas céanna ar an dá ghné. Tá duine eagraithe, críochnúil agus iontaofa á lorg ag Ollscoil Mhá Nuad le feidhmiú mar Fheidhmeannach Riaracháin do Theastas Eorpach na Gaeilge (TEG). Beidh an té a cheapfar freagrach do Stiúrthóir TEG. Tuarastal Cúntóir Feidhmiúcháin (2026): €32,855 - €49,419 (pointe 1-13) De réir fhorálacha pá na hearnála poiblí a dhéanfar ceapacháin. Dáta deiridh: 23:30 (am na hÉireann) Domhnach 8 Samhain 2026. Caithfear iarratais a chur isteach faoin dáta deiridh agus faoin am a shonraítear thuas. Cealóidh an córas go huathoibríoch iarratais atá fós idir lámha ag an am deiridh ar an dáta deiridh sonraithe. Ní ghlacfar le hiarratais mhalla. Is fostóir comhionannas deiseanna é Ollscoil Mhá Nuad Tá an post seo faoi réir Reachtanna na hOllscoile"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/nuimrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=044263": {
      "title": "Head of Communications (Specified Purpose Contract)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/10/2026 Job Title : Head Of Communications Department : External Relations Office Vacancy ID : 044263 Closing Date : 18-Oct-2026 We are seeking an experienced Head of Communications with a strong track record in media/public relations to enhance the reputation of Maynooth University during a time of exciting change, growth and innovation. The role includes the management of external and internal communications, media relations, and strategic message development and implementation across myriad audiences, stakeholders and vehicles. The appointee will report to the Director of Strategic Communications and Marketing and work closely and collegially within the Communications, Marketing, and Digital team, as well as with colleagues from the Development, Alumni Relations teams, and colleagues from across the wider University community. Senior Administration IV (2026) Salary Scale: €71,441 - €113,43p.a.(7 points) Appointments will be made in accordance with public sector pay provisions. Closing Date: 23:30hrs (local Irish time) on Sunday, 18th October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified above. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. Late applications will not be accepted. Maynooth University is an equal opportunities employer The position is subject to the Statutes of the University"
